The googlesql/ and bigquery/ .zon spec files in this directory are generated by
tools/spec_import.py from goccy/googlesqlite, pinned at:

    https://github.com/goccy/googlesqlite
    tag v0.3.1, commit 36f6275991c003cde752014fa886eae33df6615d
    testdata/specs/**.yaml

googlesqlite is MIT licensed, Copyright (c) 2026 Masaaki Goshima.

The expected values in those specs are in turn derived from the GoogleSQL
reference documentation — the SQL statements and their printed result tables in
each function's "Examples" section:

    https://github.com/google/googlesql/tree/master/docs

That documentation is published by Google under the Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0 License, and its code samples under the Apache License 2.0:

    https://developers.google.com/terms/site-policies

Portions of these files are reproduced from work created and shared by Google
and used according to terms described in the Creative Commons 4.0 Attribution
License.

The Spanner dialect (118 upstream specs) is not imported; this engine targets
BigQuery.

googlesql/compliance/ is the exception within googlesql/: it is imported from
GoogleSQL's own compliance test suite,

    https://github.com/google/googlesql
    googlesql/compliance/testdata/*.test, at the commit third_party/googlesql
    is pinned to

which is licensed under the Apache License 2.0, Copyright Google LLC. The SQL
and expected results are reproduced from it, converted to ZON and filtered to
the cases this engine supports.

zigquery/ is not covered by any of the above. It is this engine's own
regression suite, with its own NOTICE; spec_import.py neither writes it nor
counts it as drift.

To re-sync against a newer upstream (and update the commit recorded above):

    uv run --with pyyaml tools/spec_import.py --src <checkout>
    uv run --with pyyaml tools/spec_import.py --src <checkout> --check
